{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Fleetwood Mac, Hall & Oates, and Stevie Nicks fit my current interest in familiar melodies, expressive vocals, and classic pop-rock collections.",
    "The greatest-hits selections connect naturally with my repeated interest in best-of albums from Simon & Garfunkel, Melanie, and other older favorites."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Journey fits my classic-rock interests, but I would pass today because I want softer songs; Talking Heads' angular rhythms and B.B. King's blues are also less suited to that mood.",
    "The Lumineers could appeal through my interest in folk, but I currently prefer older hits collections. Unforgettable and Love Story give me too little information about the performers to judge their fit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Being an older rock act or having a greatest-hits album does not by itself make something match the melodic, softer listening I want today.",
    "My interest in folk and singer-songwriters does not mean I am equally ready to choose an unfamiliar contemporary folk album."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Harmonies, memorable melodies, and softer vocals matter more to my choice today than a broad connection to classic rock.",
    "I distinguish between music that generally suits me and what I would choose now: Journey and Kenny Loggins fit my taste, but Fleetwood Mac interests me more today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in classic hits collections but only partly captured my current preference for softer, melodic pop and folk-rock."
}"}
